## Problem 1 — the numbers, honestly

Edit `ex1/solution.ts`. Implement:

```ts
export interface MemoryReport {
  heapUsed: number;
  heapTotal: number;
  heapLimit: number;
  external: number;
  arrayBuffers: number;
  rss: number;
  nonHeapRss: number;        // rss - heapTotal, floored at 0
  heapPressure: number;      // heapUsed / heapLimit, 0..1
  status: "ok" | "warn" | "critical";
}

export function readMemoryReport(): MemoryReport
```

Read `process.memoryUsage()` and `v8.getHeapStatistics()`. `heapLimit` is
`heap_size_limit`. `status` is `"critical"` at a `heapPressure` of 0.9 or
above, `"warn"` at 0.75 or above, `"ok"` otherwise.

`nonHeapRss` approximates everything that is not the JavaScript heap — native
modules, buffers, fragmentation, the code itself — which is where you look
when the heap is healthy and the container is not.

```ts
const report = readMemoryReport();
report.heapPressure < 1;      // always
report.status;                // "ok" on a freshly started process
```

```
uv run dojo test node v3nc04_memory_leaks ex1
```

references.solution.ts:
// v3nc04_memory_leaks / ex1 - reference solution (author only, used by `dojo verify`).
import v8 from "node:v8";

export interface MemoryReport {
  heapUsed: number;
  heapTotal: number;
  heapLimit: number;
  external: number;
  arrayBuffers: number;
  rss: number;
  nonHeapRss: number;
  heapPressure: number;
  status: "ok" | "warn" | "critical";
}

export function readMemoryReport(): MemoryReport {
  const usage = process.memoryUsage();
  // snake_case because these come straight from V8's C++ struct.
  const stats = v8.getHeapStatistics();
  const heapLimit = stats.heap_size_limit;

  // The only warning you get: crossing this limit aborts the process with
  // "FATAL ERROR: Reached heap limit", which no try/catch can see.
  const heapPressure = heapLimit > 0 ? usage.heapUsed / heapLimit : 0;

  return {
    heapUsed: usage.heapUsed,
    heapTotal: usage.heapTotal,
    heapLimit,
    external: usage.external,
    arrayBuffers: usage.arrayBuffers,
    rss: usage.rss,
    // An approximation, useful as a trend and meaningless as an absolute:
    // buffers, native modules and fragmentation all land here, and none of
    // them appear in a heap snapshot.
    nonHeapRss: Math.max(0, usage.rss - usage.heapTotal),
    heapPressure,
    status: heapPressure >= 0.9 ? "critical" : heapPressure >= 0.75 ? "warn" : "ok",
  };
}

