## Problem 2 — reading a snapshot

Edit `ex2/solution.ts`. Implement:

```ts
export interface HeapNode {
  index: number;        // node ordinal, 0-based
  id: number;
  type: string;         // resolved from meta.node_types[0]
  name: string;         // resolved from the strings table
  selfSize: number;
  edgeCount: number;
  firstEdge: number;    // index into the edges array (in edge records, not integers)
}

export interface ParsedSnapshot {
  nodes: HeapNode[];
  edgeFieldCount: number;
  edges: number[];
  strings: string[];
}

export function parseSnapshot(json: string): ParsedSnapshot
```

The format is column-oriented. `snapshot.meta.node_fields` names the columns
of the flat `nodes` array — you must read the positions of `type`, `name`,
`id`, `self_size` and `edge_count` from it rather than hard-coding indices,
because the field list has changed between V8 versions.

`firstEdge` is the running total of every previous node's `edge_count`: the
prefix sum every snapshot parser has to build.

```ts
const parsed = parseSnapshot(await readFile("heap.heapsnapshot", "utf8"));
parsed.nodes[0].name;          // "(GC roots)" typically
parsed.nodes[0].firstEdge;     // 0
```

```
uv run dojo test node v3nc04_memory_leaks ex2
```

exercises.hints:
## Hint 1

Nothing in this format is self-describing except `meta`. Read
`meta.node_fields` first, find the index of each field name you need, and use
those indices as offsets into every node's record.

Hard-coding `nodes[i * 6 + 1]` works today and breaks on the next V8 that adds
a column.

## Hint 2

```ts
const fields: string[] = snapshot.meta.node_fields;
const stride = fields.length;
const at = (name: string) => fields.indexOf(name);
const nameIdx = at("name");
// node k's name string:
strings[nodes[k * stride + nameIdx]];
```

`type` is an index too, into `meta.node_types[0]` — an array of type names
like `"hidden"`, `"array"`, `"string"`, `"object"`, `"closure"`.

## Hint 3

The prefix sum is one accumulator in the same loop:

```ts
let firstEdge = 0;
for (let k = 0; k < nodeCount; k++) {
  // ... read fields ...
  result.push({ ..., firstEdge });
  firstEdge += edgeCount;
}
```

The decision left to you: whether to keep `edges` as the raw flat array or
decode it too. Decoding every edge eagerly doubles your memory for a file that
is already enormous — think about who needs it and when.

references.solution.ts:
// v3nc04_memory_leaks / ex2 - reference solution (author only, used by `dojo verify`).

export interface HeapNode {
  index: number;
  id: number;
  type: string;
  name: string;
  selfSize: number;
  edgeCount: number;
  firstEdge: number;
}

export interface ParsedSnapshot {
  nodes: HeapNode[];
  edgeFieldCount: number;
  edges: number[];
  strings: string[];
}

export function parseSnapshot(json: string): ParsedSnapshot {
  const raw = JSON.parse(json) as {
    snapshot: { meta: { node_fields: string[]; node_types: unknown[]; edge_fields: string[] } };
    nodes: number[];
    edges: number[];
    strings: string[];
  };

  const fields = raw.snapshot.meta.node_fields;
  const stride = fields.length;
  // Read the column positions from meta: the field list has gained columns
  // between V8 versions, and hard-coded offsets silently decode garbage.
  const typeIdx = fields.indexOf("type");
  const nameIdx = fields.indexOf("name");
  const idIdx = fields.indexOf("id");
  const sizeIdx = fields.indexOf("self_size");
  const edgeCountIdx = fields.indexOf("edge_count");
  const nodeTypes = (raw.snapshot.meta.node_types[0] as string[]) ?? [];

  const nodes: HeapNode[] = [];
  const count = Math.floor(raw.nodes.length / stride);
  // Each node's edges are the next edge_count records, so "where do node k's
  // edges start" is the running total of everything before it.
  let firstEdge = 0;

  for (let k = 0; k < count; k++) {
    const base = k * stride;
    const edgeCount = raw.nodes[base + edgeCountIdx];
    nodes.push({
      index: k,
      id: raw.nodes[base + idIdx],
      type: nodeTypes[raw.nodes[base + typeIdx]] ?? "unknown",
      name: raw.strings[raw.nodes[base + nameIdx]] ?? "",
      selfSize: raw.nodes[base + sizeIdx],
      edgeCount,
      firstEdge,
    });
    firstEdge += edgeCount;
  }

  return {
    nodes,
    edgeFieldCount: raw.snapshot.meta.edge_fields.length,
    // Left flat on purpose: an object per edge would multiply the memory cost
    // of a file that is already larger than the heap it describes.
    edges: raw.edges,
    strings: raw.strings,
  };
}

